<div class="process-flow">
    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-3">
        <div class="card-header">
            <span class="fw-semibold">How a submission travels the highway</span>
        </div>

        <div class="card-body">
            <p class="text-body-secondary">
                Every media item makes the same round trip: submitted to the public intake,
                ingested and stored by the internal service, re-published as a new release, then
                delivered back to this chat by an ordinary REST listener — the same path any other
                subscriber sees.
            </p>

            <ol class="process-flow-steps mb-3">
                <li>
                    An event is submitted to the <strong>Submit API</strong>
                    (<code>POST /submit</code>) from Postman, cURL, or this app's chat box.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The <strong>ExternalMediaItemService</strong> validates the submission — the
                    participant id and secret are <strong>mandatory</strong> and are read from the
                    request headers, never from the body.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The content is emitted onto the
                    <code class="process-flow-address">NFlix-ExternalContributions</code> event
                    address on EventHighway as an <code>ExternalMediaItemAdded</code> event, whose
                    credentials EventHighway verifies.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The <strong>InternalMediaService</strong> listens on
                    <code class="process-flow-address">NFlix-ExternalContributions</code> and
                    receives the content from EventHighway through an internal
                    <strong>DelegateEventHandler</strong> — the content only, never the credentials.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The InternalMediaService validates the content and submits the item to storage
                    (storage broker &rarr; SQL).
                </li>
                <li>
                    The InternalMediaService emits a <code>MediaItemAdded</code> event onto the
                    <code class="process-flow-address">NFlix-NewReleases</code> address.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Several listeners sit on <code class="process-flow-address">NFlix-NewReleases</code>;
                    the <strong>SubstrateApi</strong> listener carries a
                    <strong>REST API delegate</strong> that submits the content to the
                    <strong>Receive API</strong> (<code>POST /receive</code>). The others —
                    SofaBox, Joe, Ann and FlakyBox — each do their own thing with the same release.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The Receive API takes the content, processes it, and surfaces it on the
                    <strong>chat UI</strong>.
                </li>
            </ol>

            <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                Addresses validated against <code>SeedIdentifiers</code>:
                <code class="process-flow-address">NFlix-ExternalContributions</code> is the public
                intake the InternalMediaService alone subscribes to;
                <code class="process-flow-address">NFlix-NewReleases</code> is where it re-publishes,
                and where every downstream listener — this chat included — is bound.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-3">
        <div class="card-header">
            <span class="fw-semibold">Process flow</span>
        </div>

        <div class="card-body">
            @* Owned by processFlow.js: rendered empty here so Blazor never diffs against the
               injected SVG. The min-height in the scoped CSS holds the space until it lands. *@
            <div @ref="this.flowElement" class="process-flow-diagram"></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-header">
            <span class="fw-semibold">Sequence</span>
        </div>

        <div class="card-body">
            <div @ref="this.sequenceElement" class="process-flow-diagram"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
